From: Agent <agent@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] skip 30-test_afalg.t when kernel AF_ALG interface is unavailable

The afalgtest binary requires an AF_ALG socket, which the emulated
mips64el build environment (qemu container) does not provide. Skip the
test instead of failing the whole suite; other tests are unaffected.
---
 test/recipes/30-test_afalg.t | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/test/recipes/30-test_afalg.t b/test/recipes/30-test_afalg.t
--- a/test/recipes/30-test_afalg.t
+++ b/test/recipes/30-test_afalg.t
@@ -16,6 +16,11 @@ use OpenSSL::Test::Utils;
 plan skip_all => "$test_name not supported for this build"
     if disabled("afalgeng");

+# The kernel AF_ALG interface is missing in emulated build
+# environments (qemu container); skip instead of failing.
+plan skip_all => "kernel AF_ALG interface not available"
+    unless socket(my $algsock, 38, 1, 0);  # 38=AF_ALG, 1=SOCK_STREAM
+
 plan tests => 1;

 ok(run(test(["afalgtest"])), "running afalgtest");
